            <div xml:id="d76">

                <pb facs="0250" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89 Lithuania/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Estonia, Latvia, and Lithuania</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Coleman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-07-30T15:00:00+01:36"><hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1924—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 3:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>118. <hi rendition="#italic">In re</hi> Lithuanian debt to the United States,
                    Lithuanian Government inquires whether the United States Government would
                    protest the ratification by the Lithuanian Assembly of the trade agreement with
                    Germany which provides for the mutual cancelation of all claims arising out of
                    the war, the German occupation, reparations and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post-bellum</hi> supplies, etc. Agreement now before the Assembly. Prompt
                    reply desired.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Coleman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
